# Olympicenyl radical chain (C19H11 units linked by single C-C bonds, alternating up/down).
# One site per radical: the central edge carbon of the three-ring side (the dot in the drawing),
# the atom with most weight in the two radical bands around E_F (isolated by ~1.3 eV).
# The glide (mirror + half period) makes the A-B bond inside the cell and the B-A' bond to the
# next cell equivalent: one hopping t. A-A' and B-B' (next cell) are the second neighbours.
bands 0 1
site A atom 1
site B atom 20
onsite A e
onsite B e
hop A B 0 t
hop B A 1 t
hop A A 1 t2
hop B B 1 t2
